WEBVTT

00:16:59.527 --> 00:17:01.556
of what we're all doing day to day.

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:03.533
I wouldn't normally have shared with them

00:17:03.557 --> 00:17:07.836
that I am building a gigantic
LEGO with my stepson,

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:10.093
and that's something that they know,

00:17:10.117 --> 00:17:12.361
and I think we're actually, in some ways,

00:17:12.385 --> 00:17:15.168
more in touch with one another
than we ever have been.

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:19.100
AG: There's evidence that when we gain
this kind of personal knowledge

00:17:19.124 --> 00:17:21.092
about our colleagues' lives outside work,

00:17:21.116 --> 00:17:22.284
it humanizes them.

00:17:22.308 --> 00:17:25.006
We trust them more
and feel more similar to them.

00:17:25.030 --> 00:17:28.576
If we only talk about work,
we miss out on that information.

00:17:28.600 --> 00:17:31.786
So Alex has been experimenting
with unstructured interaction